\title "Boom-chick"
\subtitle "Guitar (standard tuning), G major chord shape"
\copyright "Pattern under MIT or Apache-2.0."
\tempo 90
\tuning E4 B3 G3 D3 A2 E2
.
// The rhythmic backbone of country, folk, and old-time guitar
// accompaniment. "Boom" = a single bass note, "chick" = a brush
// across the top strings of the chord. The bass alternates
// between the root (low G, string 6 fret 3) and the 5th (open D,
// string 4) for forward motion.
//
// Hold a standard open-G shape: 3 2 0 0 0 3 (low → high). All the
// notation below assumes that fretting hand is set; the drill is
// rhythmic.
//
//   col 0  bass G        (3.6)
//   col 1  brush top     (3.1 0.2 0.3)
//   col 2  bass D (5th)  (0.4)
//   col 3  brush top
//   col 4  bass G
//   col 5  brush top
//   col 6  bass D
//   col 7  brush top
:8 3.6 (3.1 0.2 0.3) 0.4 (3.1 0.2 0.3) 3.6 (3.1 0.2 0.3) 0.4 (3.1 0.2 0.3) |
:8 3.6 (3.1 0.2 0.3) 0.4 (3.1 0.2 0.3) 3.6 (3.1 0.2 0.3) 0.4 (3.1 0.2 0.3) |
